+# Fish respond to a nearby greeting
+
+The clean fish tank already has the wave interaction profile, but its two fish remain still while the pet greets them. Add one brief tail response during that existing action phase. No new interaction command, contact/reach, route, chore/health change, speech, sound or saved state.
+
+Expose an optional responseObjectId on Room, set by LivingRoom only for an active interact/action/wave. Room additionally gates the response class to the matching visible clean fish-tank object. Orient, walking, settle, dirty stages, other furniture, hidden/ghost objects, sick/away and reduced-motion visits have no fish greeting. Keep the class on the outer placed-object wrapper so memoized PlacedArt does not redraw on pet frames; class identity across incidental parent renders/coalesced invitations does not restart CSS. Existing suppression/reduction validates and clears the interaction synchronously. OS CSS also disables the response defensively.
+
+Wrap only each fish's existing tail path in a fish-tail group; preserve the existing fish translation, rotation, scale, water/glass layers and clipping. Tail pivot is its attached right-edge midpoint (fill-box100%50%); the body ellipse covers the root. One1400ms damped CSS oscillation matches ACTION_MS.wave, returns to neutral, and never repeats. Red amplitude<=10degrees; yellow opposite<=6.5degrees. No delay beyond the finite action, no autonomous loop and no additional JS RAF/timer/subscription. Parent interaction cancellation removes the class; tiny tail motion may snap to neutral on cancellation, so measure actual visual bounds and review native samples rather than claim blended cancellation. Normal completion returns continuously to zero.
+
+Before implementation, archive unanimated tank renders for3stages/4rotations/2raster sizes and require exact pixel equality after the tail wrappers. Red tests exercise real Room and LivingRoom: only chosen clean tank/action, phase deadlines, coalescing/no extra frame owner or Room redraws, player interruption, live OS/device reduction, sick/away, stage/target changes, hidden elapsed expiry and no replay. Native tests use actual CSS animation inventory/timing/target styles, both outer rotations, stationary water/body transforms, all three pet species and exact save tables. Sample finite CSS currentTime deterministically only in disposable test contexts; separately wait for real native completion. Stills must record paused CSS sampling rather than disabling that effect. Inspect tail attachment/bounds/clipping and room/bubble clearance before one bounded independent review.
+
+Broad continuing user authorization covers this visual interaction detail. Prepare new design/red/baseline paths while creator-tools is frozen; production Room/LivingRoom/fish/CSS and ART edits wait for that checkpoint. Heavy work remains sequential/capped with2GiB reserve; no CPU/battery savings claim or physical-device/AT/human-temporal-comfort certification.
+
+Preparation correction before implementation: sick/away tests now allow the existing120ms resident join to finish before asserting0RAF, while fish response removal remains immediate. Initial10resident red cases all failed at the absent response before reaching that assertion; exact original red bytes retained. No reduction/response bound relaxed. Static candidate comparison24/24pixel+PNGexact passes, and the applied tail source hash must equal that tested candidate.
+
+Late-frame refinement: record the time of each existing semantic draw in Shown and derive one negative CSS delay from the action's absolute start. The held draw time keeps that delay stable on repeated invitations and ordinary frames. A new late-first-frame regression fails for absent -640ms offset before the fix, then passes alongside all existing phase/clock tests. No extra frame loop or timer. The first late-red command used an unsupported Vitest minWorkers option and did not run a test; the corrected distinct red-v2 command failed at the intended missing offset.
+
+Native harness investigation: the initial seven failures comprised six sampling-handle errors and an invalid landscape room-width assumption. Terminal currentTime1400 legitimately removes the effect from document.getAnimations; a fresh query could not rewind it for a peak capture. Retain test-only handles across deterministic samples, assert their actual restored native effects at the peak, and check repeated invitations before terminal sampling. The landscape camera preserves its existing189.95px room width in a424x232px viewport; enforce the existing90px canvas minimum instead of imposing a200px individual room minimum. Native real completion/reduction/cross-tab/player cancellation already passed. Initial captures are historical, not final peak evidence. Final sampling subtracts each measured native CSS delay to address the intended elapsed keyframe phase.
